From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:07:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 096/144] GreatDANE: privacy-manifest and README honesty fixes
 (NGD round 2 M4, L1, L4, L6)

- PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy comment and PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md: replace "Dane's own servers receive nothing".
  - Say what pepecoin.surf actually sees: the update check's request fields plus IP, and pages the user opens.
  - Default-tile icons are bundled (tippytop), so the new-tab page contacts none of those sites.
  - User-initiated loads of Dane sites are ordinary browsing.
- L1: the CA92.1 rationale now openly lists other-app preference domains Gecko uses:
  - the com.apple.dock persistent-domain read (nsMacDockSupport.mm:367, :407) and write (:347);
  - the com.apple.loginwindow TALLogoutSavesState read (nsCocoaUtils.mm:310-312).
  Callers are named. The manifest values are unchanged.
- L6: OtherDiagnosticData purposes are now AppFunctionality + Analytics.
- L4: greatdane/README.md gets a known regression: system passkeys (Touch ID / iCloud Keychain via
  public-key-credential) are unavailable until Apple grants the entitlement and a provisioning profile is embedded.
- README: the signing notes now match the round-2 signer (main-executable-only exception, case-insensitive
  realpath guard with a /Volumes allowlist, identity redaction, signing.conf, in-tree sign-only.sh).
